This product includes a modified Java port of the xunazo AZO decoder for
extraction-only EGG method-3 payload support. xunazo is distributed under the
zlib license and is credited in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md and in the source file
that contains the modified port.

Third-party dependency notices are maintained in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.
The separate libreadwide-lzham.so target uses the pinned MIT LZHAM decoder/common
subset with marked local safety changes and a Readwide Apache-2.0 Java/JNI adapter.
Its private NDK C++ runtime retains LLVM/legacy MIT notices. Keep the APK assets
open_source_licenses/lzham_mit.txt and open_source_licenses/llvm_cxx_runtime.txt.
Source provenance and original/local hashes are in third_party/lzham.
The independent libreadwide-ppmd.so target uses eight unchanged public-domain
7-Zip Ppmd8 decoder/platform files with a Readwide Apache-2.0 Java/JNI adapter.
Source declarations and hashes are retained in third_party/ppmd8; the APK includes
assets/open_source_licenses/ppmd8_public_domain.txt. No encoder or UnRAR code is
included. Its libarchive ZIP regression resources and BSD notices are test-only.
The source build includes a separate LGPL-2.1-only libreadwide-cab.so target using
libmspack's CAB decoder and a Readwide JNI adapter, with a marked strict-continuation
change in cabd.c. License/provenance are retained in third_party/libmspack; the APK
includes assets/open_source_licenses/libmspack_cab_lgpl_2_1.txt with the full license
and relinking notice. App routes are connected in source; native execution remains pending. See
THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md. Attributed regression resources are test-only.
The APK also packages the exact libarchive-android/native-codec terms at
assets/open_source_licenses/libarchive_android_and_codecs.txt, the full
XADMaster WinZip JPEG LGPL-2.1 text at
assets/open_source_licenses/xadmaster_winzip_jpeg_lgpl_2_1.txt, and the
WavPack BSD-3-Clause notice at
assets/open_source_licenses/wavpack_bsd_3_clause.txt.
